A||||9||Blacktree||Fastback tail lights on a coupe?||||1||
Z||000000||Blacktree||12-13-2001||02:33 AM||||I think the fastback tail lights look SO much better than the notchback tail lights. BUT, I don't want to convert my coupe to a fastback just for the tail lights (I like the notchback look). The only way I can think of to accomplish this and not have the car look like @$$ would be to get a fastback engine lid, tail lights, and rear clip and somehow graft the rear part of the fastback clip (just behind the sail panels) onto the notchback clip. Then install the fastback engine lid and tail lights as normal.<P>Or maybe there are some fastback-taillights-on-a-notchback kits that I don't know of (crossing my fingers)?<p>[This message has been edited by Blacktree (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
